        "thought_text": "Focus on edge weights and connectivity: The previous approach of removing edges with high weights might not be optimal. Instead, we should focus on removing edges that, when removed, disconnect the graph or create cycles that don't contribute to the shortest paths. This approach should help maximize the number of good vertices while respecting the constraint of keeping at most k edges. Additionally, we should consider the connectivity of the graph and ensure that the remaining edges form a tree structure to maintain the shortest path property.",
